<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 3-mth T-bills 99 pct sold,yielding 85 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 3-mth T-bills 99 pct sold,yielding 85 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 6.7 billion levs of three-month floater coupon T-bills was 99.18 percent sold, yielding 85.19 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 20 percent monthly or 240 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		    BG 3020096023</p>
<p> Par value			 6.7 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		    October 28, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			October 30, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		   January 29, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		   6,700 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	     86.12 percent</p>
<p> Bids approved		   6,645 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	    86.31 percent</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity   85.19 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
